  "body": "**What.** Make `amp_flint_par.py`'s result independent of `--procs`: `_products` adds each order's products per group in task order, as `I236-win2/amp_flint_par_fixsum.py` does. Measure its wall-time cost against the current code on an idle machine at K 25 and K 33, with 2 and 4 workers. Recommended by win2 in #236's summary.\n\n**Why.** #236 showed that, with the sum in task order, `--procs` 1, 2, 3 and 4 give the same bits at K 25, equal to the current `--procs 1`. The current code differs in its last digits between counts (#229: \u03c3\u2081\u2086 of K 33 by 1.5e-19). Bit-for-bit comparisons across machines and runs then need no matching count. Under load the variant cost 12\u201325% more wall time, measured beside other jobs.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).**\n- With the change, `--procs` 1\u20134 at K 25 give equal bits, and the change equals the current `--procs 1` file.\n- The clean timing is reported. Whether to adopt the change at that cost is decided on it.\n\n**Depends on.** #236.\n",
