   "body": "Coordinator: done, with option C (Nathan's choice), not #236's per-task sum. Workers sum fixed blocks of tasks (NBLOCK = 12), and the main adds the block sums in block order (main 64914d8; AGENTS.md updated in 6f41463).\n\n**Test** (Mac, \u03c9/\u03c9\u221e = 1.10, K 17, J 200, 640 bits, `--fit phys --mf 6:12`; comparison drops timing keys and `procs`, and catches a one-digit change in a copy):\n\n| pair | result |\n|---|---|\n| previous code, `--procs` 1 against 3 | 37 differing entries, first `f/17_11` (the test can fail) |\n| new code, `--procs` 1 against 2, 3 and 4 | equal bit for bit (all three) |\n| previous code against new, `--procs` 1 | 32 differing entries, as expected: the sum is associated differently |\n\n**Product time** at this size: 27.3, 11.9, 14.8 and 7.1 s for 1\u20134 workers. The machine was shared, and fits take 95% of the total here. A production timing comes from the next K 33+ run.\n\n**Deviation from the acceptance:** the new bits do not equal the previous `--procs 1` file, by design of option C. Files from before 64914d8 compare bit for bit only at the same `--procs` and with that code. #228 and #256 run the previous code, which they need for comparing with #82.\n\n**Aside:** in this small case the previous code's \u03c3 differ by up to 4.6e-3 relative between 1 and 3 workers from n = 8 on. At J 200 the late-order fits amplify rounding. At J 1000\u20131500 the same differences are 1e-19 or below (#229, #236).",
